WEBVTT

00:02.920 --> 00:04.380
Did you just shoot a dead body?!

00:05.000 --> 00:06.750
<b>World of Nox Ryugasaki</b>

00:05.000 --> 00:06.750
<b>78509 subscribers</b>

00:05.000 --> 00:06.750
<b>2054 watching now
Superhero Vtubr Nox Ryugasaki's EXOPRIMAL livestream!
Subscribe to my channel!</b>

00:05.000 --> 00:06.750
You are so going down!

00:11.420 --> 00:13.170
<b>YUNA: Can't wait
Poteo: Why so many viewers?
Hosogai: What's with all the people today?
Haracchi: Kiui Watase?
Zacchi: ROFLMAO
Anne: Is something up?
Strong as usual</b>

00:17.170 --> 00:19.920
Aw, man! That's it for today!

00:20.880 --> 00:21.710
<b>LMAOOOO
I'm a fan
Kiui Watase? Lol
Why?</b>

00:23.460 --> 00:24.710
<b>Blocked words</b>

00:23.460 --> 00:24.710
<b>Watase</b>

00:23.750 --> 00:24.710
<b>Kiui</b>

00:26.540 --> 00:29.000
So yeah, goodbye world!

00:32.330 --> 00:37.250
When will I be able to use magic?

00:37.380 --> 00:42.130
I've always longed for something special

00:42.420 --> 00:47.290
1, 2, 3, fall in line, B, C, D, eagerly obedient

00:47.420 --> 00:52.880
But I know best, that that's not me

00:53.750 --> 00:59.460
No one thinks this is ok the way it is

00:59.460 --> 01:02.250
Anxious legs weighing me down

01:03.290 --> 01:06.960
Even you, who I hold so close

01:07.080 --> 01:11.670
Being frustratingly out of reach, what I see is...

01:11.920 --> 01:17.540
A variety of colors, a myriad of brightness

01:17.540 --> 01:22.540
Even if I've been fed up countless times -resonating with you-

01:22.750 --> 01:27.500
Breaking through my thoughts that seem to be on a loop

01:27.500 --> 01:32.130
Mayday to these melancholic days, I dance in the air

01:32.130 --> 01:36.790
Taking a bite out of the gloomy sky

01:36.960 --> 01:44.790
There's an unexpected sweetness, amidst the bitter, sour, salty taste

01:47.130 --> 01:53.880
I'm moving towards where the light shines

02:01.580 --> 02:02.920
I don't want it to end.

02:02.330 --> 02:06.460
<b>Kimura's
legendary livestream</b>

02:02.330 --> 02:06.460
<b>Certified Banger</b>

02:02.420 --> 02:06.460
<b>Episode 11: What I Love</b>

02:03.290 --> 02:06.880
JUST NO!

02:06.880 --> 02:08.920
This is so embarrassing!

02:09.250 --> 02:11.830
Umm, what does this "M" mean?

02:09.580 --> 02:11.580
How could I? How could I do this?!

02:12.000 --> 02:13.710
2.2 million views.

02:13.710 --> 02:15.380
2.2 million?!

02:15.710 --> 02:17.130
That blew up like crazy.

02:17.710 --> 02:18.880
I should file a report...

02:18.880 --> 02:19.580
Nuh-uh!

02:20.040 --> 02:24.210
Wh-why?! At this rate the whole world
will hear my singing!

02:24.460 --> 02:26.170
But we can't waste the attention.

02:26.170 --> 02:27.830
Besides, look.

02:28.210 --> 02:32.960
<b>Oyaki
I don't even know this group and I cried
Sakura
When's the full version of the song coming?</b>

02:28.580 --> 02:32.250
Are these... comments from viewers?

02:32.000 --> 02:32.960
<b>This is real heartfelt drama</b>

02:33.460 --> 02:36.130
No one's making fun of you, Mei.

02:36.420 --> 02:37.460
Nono-tan...

02:39.040 --> 02:41.080
So close. I'm in love.

02:41.670 --> 02:43.130
Will you look at the screen?

02:44.630 --> 02:49.750
So yeah, I really want to finish this song properly.

02:50.250 --> 02:53.210
I agree. It's such a good song.

02:53.830 --> 02:57.330
But without Mahiru, we can't
make a music video, y'know?

02:57.670 --> 02:58.540
That okay with you?

02:59.040 --> 03:01.080
Yeah... That's true.

03:01.790 --> 03:04.500
But Mahiru's pushing ahead right now.

03:05.080 --> 03:07.500
So we should move forward, too.

03:08.710 --> 03:10.210
But Nono-tan?

03:10.420 --> 03:11.250
Huh?

03:11.630 --> 03:13.880
Are you sure you're ready to sing?

03:14.960 --> 03:17.130
I don't know if I can sing properly.

03:19.130 --> 03:20.250
I dunno.

03:21.540 --> 03:22.330
But hey.

03:23.710 --> 03:25.960
That's part of the challenge, right?

03:28.130 --> 03:28.880
Yeah.

03:38.830 --> 03:39.630
These won't do.

03:40.000 --> 03:40.580
Huh?

03:41.130 --> 03:45.710
They're completely devoid of the appeal
I saw in Yoru Umitsuki's art.

03:46.790 --> 03:49.170
Yoru Umitsuki's art?

03:51.210 --> 03:56.460
Let's see. Miss Yoru, what about
these drawing do you like?

03:57.920 --> 03:59.000
Um, well...

04:03.080 --> 04:05.290
F-for example, here.

04:05.580 --> 04:08.380
I'm happy with how the body is angled here.

04:08.880 --> 04:09.830
What else?

04:10.170 --> 04:11.880
A-and...

04:12.210 --> 04:14.040
This eye over here...doesn't look flat.

04:14.500 --> 04:18.790
And the creases in the clothes I drew from life-

04:18.790 --> 04:19.830
I see what it is.

04:21.210 --> 04:25.210
You don't like your own art, do you?

04:28.750 --> 04:30.880
Okay, here goes the camera test!

04:31.330 --> 04:34.790
love, love, weather

04:35.460 --> 04:37.000
lovely weather

04:37.000 --> 04:40.290
Everything surely is lovely weather

04:38.330 --> 04:39.250
Wow.

04:39.250 --> 04:43.750
For the actual show, we'll use this to sync
the virtual Sundolls so they dance in real time.

04:42.750 --> 04:45.790
Manipulating even the sun (just might be unbeatable)

04:45.790 --> 04:47.750
The world is the backdrop

04:47.710 --> 04:50.580
This is where they'll use my designs...

04:48.130 --> 04:50.750
Because when rain would be more lovely

04:50.750 --> 04:51.500
Make it rain...

04:51.670 --> 04:53.210
Good work, everyone!

04:54.000 --> 04:57.040
Okay, Mero. Don't forget to get a receipt.

04:57.380 --> 04:58.420
Got it!

05:06.830 --> 05:08.790
So this girl and Kano...

05:09.960 --> 05:10.880
What?

05:10.880 --> 05:12.790
Huh?! No, uh...

05:13.040 --> 05:16.210
If this is about Nonoka's incident,
I can't tell you anything.

05:17.130 --> 05:20.790
I don't intend on prying about the incident.

05:21.250 --> 05:24.000
Just knowing who Kano is now is enough for me.

05:26.040 --> 05:29.380
Miss Umitsuki, do you know about LookIdiot?

05:30.250 --> 05:32.540
You mean the scandal exposing account?

05:32.830 --> 05:34.880
What are your thoughts on that?

05:37.170 --> 05:39.080
I think it's despicable.

05:40.170 --> 05:44.130
...is easy to say, but I think that
might be too self-righteous of me.

05:45.540 --> 05:48.210
Posting anonymously to hurt people...

05:48.420 --> 05:50.170
It's really an awful thing to do.

05:50.460 --> 05:53.040
But I feel like LookIdiot was kinda just...

05:53.580 --> 05:56.000
overblown griping, in a way.

05:56.420 --> 05:57.670
What do you mean by that?

05:58.210 --> 06:07.040
See, I always sucked at being true to myself at school
and just vented elsewhere to make myself feel better.

06:07.580 --> 06:09.460
And you think LookIdiot was the same?

06:10.170 --> 06:14.960
Yes. I think I managed to escape my habit of doing that,

06:15.630 --> 06:19.000
but only because I met a certain someone.

06:20.250 --> 06:25.540
If I hadn't been so fortunate I might still
be my old griping self, and given that,

06:26.000 --> 06:30.710
denouncing them completely... seems a little hypocritical.

06:33.580 --> 06:37.250
I guess Nonoka only attracts weird people or something.

06:39.000 --> 06:45.790
The computer screen I forgot to turn off...

06:48.380 --> 06:50.960
Sorry. I'm gonna stop for a moment.

06:53.500 --> 06:57.830
That just now... wasn't how Nono-tan sings.

06:59.670 --> 07:03.130
I dunno. What am I singing for, anyway?

07:05.380 --> 07:09.580
I think who you want to deliver
the song to is the important thing.

07:10.630 --> 07:11.540
"Who"?

07:12.380 --> 07:16.000
You're just following the notes and
I can't tell what your message is.

07:18.250 --> 07:21.500
That's what my piano teacher told me all the time.

07:22.380 --> 07:28.710
I always played because my parents told me to,
and I didn't even know if I liked piano or not.

07:30.000 --> 07:34.420
But after I met you, Nono-tan, that all changed.

07:38.710 --> 07:40.040
<b>Arrangement: Kimura
Vocals: Nono-tan</b>

07:40.040 --> 07:41.710
<b>Music: Kimura
Lyrics/Vocals:</b>

07:43.750 --> 07:46.670
When did you write these lyrics again?

07:47.790 --> 07:49.880
Just after our Halloween gig.

07:51.080 --> 07:52.500
Why don't we rewrite it all?

07:53.000 --> 07:53.790
Huh?

07:54.420 --> 07:58.580
All the lyrics. To what you want
to sing about now, Nono-tan.

08:07.420 --> 08:09.960
<b>Wanna study together at the diner
in front of the station tomorrow?
A bunch of us are coming
I have stuff to do so I gotta pass</b>

08:07.420 --> 08:09.960
<b>Today</b>

08:07.420 --> 08:09.960
<b>I saw you're in a band (?)
or something Mahiru! Pretty amazing.
Tell me about it sometime</b>

08:09.960 --> 08:12.540
<b>I have stuff to do so I gotta pass</b>

08:09.960 --> 08:12.540
<b>Today</b>

08:09.960 --> 08:12.540
<b>I saw you're in a band (?)
or something Mahiru! Pretty amazing.
Tell me about it sometime
Also heard from Hamauchi
that Watase's in it too,
of all people lol</b>

08:12.540 --> 08:16.540
<b>Watase's in it too</b>

08:20.000 --> 08:21.170
Thank you for coming.

08:21.330 --> 08:22.830
Th-thank you for your time.

08:23.830 --> 08:26.250
About the revised art you brought me this time.

08:27.290 --> 08:29.330
I'm sorry. You're out of time.

08:29.880 --> 08:30.540
Huh?

08:31.170 --> 08:35.170
I want to let you keep trying,
but we just don't have the time.

08:37.420 --> 08:40.080
B-but, this isn't my art at all anymore.

08:40.630 --> 08:44.830
True. But this is the only reasonable compromise
I can see as a grownup.

08:45.080 --> 08:47.040
<b>Costume and character designs:
it feels like you don't really</b>

08:45.090 --> 08:47.040
<b>love them or think they're cute
What you love and think are cute aren't coming across here.
Stop trying to draw what you think we or most people want.</b>

08:45.710 --> 08:47.130
Miss Yoru Umitsuki.

08:47.920 --> 08:49.960
Will you make those fixes as indicated?

08:52.380 --> 08:55.540
Aw, well. It's for the best, right?

08:55.920 --> 09:00.750
It'd be awful if I didn't make the deadline,
but I just have to fix this the way they want!

09:01.130 --> 09:04.380
Yeah, okay. So it won't be my art anymore,

09:04.380 --> 09:07.830
but I'll meet the deadline and I'm safe, it's all good!

09:12.420 --> 09:14.290
Like there's any way...

09:15.880 --> 09:17.630
...I'm okay with that.

09:28.790 --> 09:29.040
<b>A gift from the Watase Atelier of Painting
Original idea by Mahiru Kouzuki</b>

09:30.420 --> 09:33.290
<b>A gift from the Watase Atelier of Painting
Original idea by</b>

09:30.420 --> 09:33.290
<b>Yoru Umitsuki</b>

09:36.380 --> 09:39.080
Yoru Umitsuki's art... huh?

09:41.380 --> 09:45.250
I see. So she's going ahead with the new song?

09:45.630 --> 09:49.290
Yep. Though she still doesn't seem
sure what she's singing for.

09:49.710 --> 09:52.880
But she wants to catch up because
you're pushing on ahead.

09:53.540 --> 09:54.750
Kano said that?

09:59.040 --> 10:01.170
Hey, can I ask you a favor?

10:02.420 --> 10:04.830
Hmm, it's not here.

10:05.210 --> 10:06.710
The one that was used for the mural, right?

10:07.040 --> 10:11.080
Yeah. I wanted to take a look
at the original painting again.

10:11.540 --> 10:15.130
That must mean... it's in storage in Omiya.

10:15.540 --> 10:18.290
Really?! Then can we go together to-

10:19.790 --> 10:22.130
Uh. Can you just let them know ahead of time?

10:22.130 --> 10:24.130
Then I'll go look by myself.

10:25.250 --> 10:28.580
What? You're not worried for my sake, are you?

10:29.630 --> 10:32.630
Well, Omiya's a pretty small place, you know?

10:32.630 --> 10:33.960
I knew it.

10:34.460 --> 10:37.920
I mean, word about us is getting around.

10:38.460 --> 10:41.670
Did you get any messages like I did?

10:41.830 --> 10:44.830
<b>Mayumi
So everything you told us</b>

10:41.840 --> 10:44.830
<b>since middle school was a lie?
Hamauchi
Man, you're such a let down
Haracchi
Saw your livestream. Hilarious lmao</b>

10:42.210 --> 10:44.630
Nope. Not that I know of.

10:46.250 --> 10:47.000
Really?

10:47.000 --> 10:47.880
<b>Miyahara Kita Elementary Class 6-1 (37)
I feel for the poor listeners she lied to</b>

10:48.500 --> 10:50.000
<b>All of Nox Ryugasaki's stories
about being popular at school</b>

10:48.790 --> 10:50.000
Really.

10:50.250 --> 10:54.460
And I mean, even if I run into someone
I know and they mess with me,

10:54.460 --> 10:57.670
"Shut up, keep it to yourself!" is what I'll tell 'em.

10:58.420 --> 11:01.040
You know, like some punk band.

11:03.710 --> 11:04.500
Okay.

11:04.500 --> 11:05.830
You would say that, Kiui.

11:06.380 --> 11:08.460
Yeah! 'Course I would.

11:06.630 --> 11:07.040
<b>Hiding chats doesn't
delete their messages
Cancel         Hide</b>

11:07.040 --> 11:07.880
<b>Ryusei
What, are you bored? lol</b>

11:07.880 --> 11:08.290
<b>Hiding chats doesn't
delete their messages
Cancel         Hide</b>

11:08.290 --> 11:09.130
<b>Hinano
Watase, don't you have anything better to do?</b>

11:08.460 --> 11:12.580
After all, I'm an invincible superhero, remember?

11:09.130 --> 11:09.540
<b>Hiding chats doesn't
delete their messages
Cancel         Hide</b>

11:09.540 --> 11:10.130
<b>Takasato
Wow, you're a livestreamer? lmao
Let's get together with the others sometime!</b>

11:18.330 --> 11:23.380
All the lyrics. To what you want
to sing about now, Nono-tan.

11:25.330 --> 11:27.670
Oh, man! I dunno!

11:30.040 --> 11:33.380
Come on, what am I singing for?

11:33.580 --> 11:39.080
<b>Colorful Moonlight</b>

11:34.380 --> 11:37.210
Who do I want to sing for?

11:41.040 --> 11:44.500
So? Why do you suddenly want
to see your old art again?

11:44.880 --> 11:49.540
Well, I was trying to figure out if I actually like my art.

11:51.290 --> 11:52.880
You said that before, too.

11:53.630 --> 11:55.880
That you want to learn to like yourself.

11:56.540 --> 12:02.330
Yeah. But the harder I try on this project
right now, the more I feel lost.

12:04.580 --> 12:06.290
I like it, though.

12:07.170 --> 12:11.210
Huh? Y-you mean you like my art?

12:12.290 --> 12:13.080
Nah.

12:13.580 --> 12:15.210
I like the way I am!

12:16.130 --> 12:18.130
<b>Storage Space</b>

12:17.000 --> 12:18.630
Wow, this takes me back.

12:18.920 --> 12:21.250
This was the first time, you know.

12:21.250 --> 12:23.500
That I fell behind you.

12:23.960 --> 12:25.080
Was it?

12:25.790 --> 12:28.250
Aw, look at this. It's all skewed!

12:28.710 --> 12:31.000
And the colors are weird. Way too uninhibited!

12:31.000 --> 12:32.000
True.

12:32.540 --> 12:33.500
But still...

12:34.040 --> 12:36.040
It's a nice painting, isn't it?

12:40.420 --> 12:42.170
Huh? These ones here...

12:42.380 --> 12:44.790
Oh. I guess these are ones I did.

12:44.790 --> 12:45.880
It's been ages.

12:46.210 --> 12:47.880
You really were so good.

12:47.880 --> 12:49.630
Uh, this was from third grade?!

12:50.130 --> 12:54.710
Whoa! Can you believe it's the work of a
third-grader?! It's so detailed.

12:55.210 --> 12:59.420
I guess. But this really isn't anything, y'know?

13:00.250 --> 13:03.790
That's how I am. I get the knack
of things faster than anybody.

13:03.790 --> 13:07.710
I'm the best at everything at the start,
and people treat me like a hero.

13:08.250 --> 13:13.880
But then I get overtaken by the ones who
practice real hard or find passion in what they do.

13:15.830 --> 13:16.790
That's why...

13:17.750 --> 13:19.710
I always quit before I get overtaken!

13:20.000 --> 13:22.080
If I never lose, it's total victory for me!

13:22.580 --> 13:24.380
What? That's just sneaky.

13:24.710 --> 13:25.500
Look at this!

13:25.920 --> 13:29.500
Ooh, I remember this! It's my painting of you, Kiui.

13:29.830 --> 13:32.540
This game was all the rage at school, wasn't it?

13:32.920 --> 13:36.920
It sure was. I wonder if that arcade's still there?

13:38.040 --> 13:39.790
You're owning everyone here, Kiui.

13:39.790 --> 13:43.420
How strong did you think I was back then?

13:43.420 --> 13:46.420
You have to ask? You're invincible, Kiui!

13:47.670 --> 13:50.500
Back then, maybe I was.

13:57.040 --> 14:00.710
Hey, I'm thinking of stopping by this arcade as well.

14:00.710 --> 14:01.330
So tired!

14:01.330 --> 14:02.000
Yeah.

14:02.210 --> 14:02.830
Huh?

14:02.830 --> 14:03.920
I'm hungry, too.

14:03.920 --> 14:04.540
I know.

14:04.540 --> 14:05.670
I'm kinda craving pancakes.

14:05.670 --> 14:06.380
Sounds great.

14:06.380 --> 14:07.000
Right?

14:07.250 --> 14:08.080
Do you know them?

14:07.630 --> 14:08.080
Let's go!

14:08.080 --> 14:09.630
Nope, not in the slightest.

14:10.920 --> 14:12.380
Then why...

14:13.460 --> 14:14.580
Allow me to explain!

14:14.880 --> 14:17.420
When you avoid school and shut yourself away at home,

14:17.420 --> 14:22.210
the mere sight of a group clad in school uniforms is
enough to make you shy away in terror!

14:24.250 --> 14:27.130
Uh, that's where you're supposed to laugh.

14:27.960 --> 14:29.540
Hey, Kiui...

14:29.540 --> 14:30.380
Hmm?

14:30.790 --> 14:34.710
You said you didn't get messages
from anyone, but is that really true?

14:35.500 --> 14:36.420
Well...

14:40.170 --> 14:41.750
Hamauchi and Mayumi?

14:42.170 --> 14:43.580
What? These are awful.

14:43.580 --> 14:46.710
Well, I figure they never liked me to begin with.

14:47.250 --> 14:50.500
And I lied to everyone because
I didn't want to let them down.

14:50.040 --> 14:53.540
<b>Yamane
Your student council excuse</b>

14:50.040 --> 14:53.540
<b>Daichi Kitano
Student council's busier than I thought.
Wish I could go.</b>

14:50.050 --> 14:53.540
<b>for never hanging out was a lie?
Nishiguchi
Maybe next time when I pass on something
I'll say I'm busy with stuco too lol
Higashiyama
I'm swamped with the school fair.
Student council duties, y'know?</b>

14:51.080 --> 14:52.670
I'm just getting what I deserve.

14:54.830 --> 14:57.500
See, you can't change your past.

14:58.130 --> 15:03.750
I changed my looks and name and everything,
to start living a completely new life.

15:05.670 --> 15:09.710
But I get doxed once,
and it's straight back to square one.

15:10.380 --> 15:11.880
Allow me to explain!

15:12.460 --> 15:20.460
K-Kiui Watase can edit videos and even come up
with that amazing gig as JELEE's all-round super whiz!

15:16.630 --> 15:18.130
Is she dancing?

15:20.960 --> 15:25.710
Still to this day, in my eyes,
she's an ever-shining superhero!

15:28.830 --> 15:30.040
What? That's so lame.

15:30.040 --> 15:31.080
That's not nice!

15:33.170 --> 15:34.000
Thanks, though.

15:35.750 --> 15:38.210
Okay! It's off to the arcade, then!

15:38.210 --> 15:39.670
Huh? I can go alone-

15:39.670 --> 15:40.830
No worries!

15:42.960 --> 15:44.380
I don't want to run anymore.

15:49.830 --> 15:54.460
We used to come a lot on our days off with...
our friends from around here... huh?

15:54.710 --> 15:57.670
Sorry, I showed off and said I'd come along,

15:57.670 --> 16:00.000
but I'm so not ready for this, after all.

16:00.000 --> 16:01.380
Lemme run to the restroom.

16:02.170 --> 16:03.000
Uh, sure.

16:12.460 --> 16:13.040
Oh!

16:14.080 --> 16:15.250
It's still here!

16:15.250 --> 16:17.460
Oh hey! Mahiru?

16:18.750 --> 16:20.500
Hamauchi and Mayumi?!

16:20.880 --> 16:22.210
I'm here too!

16:26.290 --> 16:29.170
Hamauchi and them are here. Let's split.

16:32.460 --> 16:35.040
Dude, Mahiru. I saw the thing about JELEE!

16:35.040 --> 16:37.040
Oh... Thanks.

16:37.040 --> 16:40.710
Pretty impressive. I've been bragging
about it to my entire class.

16:41.000 --> 16:44.460
And hey, Watase's in JELEE too, right?

16:44.790 --> 16:47.710
Oh yeah, Watase. That liar.

16:48.710 --> 16:50.080
Why would you say that?!

16:50.080 --> 16:53.750
But it's true, right? She stopped
going to school, didn't she?

16:54.210 --> 16:58.880
She used to be like, everyone's leader when
we were kids, but people sure change, huh?

17:00.880 --> 17:04.000
Hey, Kiui's still as cool as ever, okay?!

17:09.380 --> 17:14.290
Oh yeah, I remember now.
You used to always tag along with her, huh?

17:14.710 --> 17:18.250
Come on, Kouzuki. You're famous now.

17:18.250 --> 17:20.710
Shouldn't you be growing out of that kind of thing?

17:21.210 --> 17:23.670
This isn't about growing out of anything.

17:24.710 --> 17:27.000
I mean, she can't go to school? How lame is that?

17:27.250 --> 17:28.460
Yeah, totally!

17:32.710 --> 17:34.580
You're invincible, Kiui!

17:37.880 --> 17:38.750
Hmm?

17:41.290 --> 17:42.130
Yo.

17:45.210 --> 17:47.290
Huh? Wait, are you Watase?!

17:47.580 --> 17:50.670
What?! You look way different now.

17:52.670 --> 17:56.210
Anyway, Watase. Why'd you block us?

17:57.040 --> 17:58.040
What she said.

17:58.330 --> 18:01.500
And here I thought we were friends. What a jerk move.

18:02.380 --> 18:06.460
Those weren't messages you'd send to a friend...

18:06.920 --> 18:09.000
What? I can't hear you.

18:09.380 --> 18:10.580
Hey. You guys!

18:11.130 --> 18:13.830
What was it again? Ryugasaki...?

18:13.830 --> 18:14.830
Nox!

18:15.250 --> 18:17.920
But that avatar acts like a guy, right?

18:17.920 --> 18:22.630
Oh! Are you like, one of those people
who actually wants to be a guy?

18:21.130 --> 18:23.500
It's not... like that...

18:23.500 --> 18:26.500
Yeah, yeah! That "diversity" stuff?
It's like a trend these days, huh?

18:27.000 --> 18:31.960
Why don't you just quit being weird
and live like a normal person?

18:33.670 --> 18:34.790
...okay?

18:35.290 --> 18:36.040
Huh?

18:36.500 --> 18:37.790
I said,

18:38.710 --> 18:40.040
I never changed!

18:41.290 --> 18:44.080
Not one bit, okay?!

18:45.000 --> 18:47.710
"Normal" people like you have no idea what it's like!

18:48.080 --> 18:51.040
To get mocked for just saying
you love the things you love!

18:51.420 --> 18:53.500
Your body keeps growing on its own,

18:53.750 --> 18:56.960
and when you wear the clothes you like people stare!

18:57.290 --> 18:59.170
You don't know how that feels!

18:59.670 --> 19:01.130
But... still!

19:01.790 --> 19:03.330
I let the world get the better of me,

19:03.330 --> 19:06.920
I couldn't even go to school and I hate myself for that!

19:07.380 --> 19:11.170
I wanted to love who I am as Kiui Watase again.

19:11.630 --> 19:14.210
I tried and tried but I couldn't!

19:14.630 --> 19:18.000
That's why my looks, my voice,

19:18.750 --> 19:22.750
my body, my personality,

19:23.420 --> 19:26.500
where I belong, my backstory...

19:26.500 --> 19:29.000
I created all that on my own so I could love myself!

19:29.250 --> 19:31.130
So don't deny me that!

19:31.130 --> 19:34.170
The guy I created, the persona I love...

19:34.330 --> 19:36.420
I won't let anyone deny that identity!

19:37.170 --> 19:41.290
I'm the unrivalled, invincible VTuber...

19:41.540 --> 19:43.130
Nox Ryugasaki!

19:43.630 --> 19:46.210
You got a problem with that?!

19:56.630 --> 20:00.170
Well... that's probably gonna get spread like wildfire.

20:00.540 --> 20:01.630
Probably.

20:03.130 --> 20:05.500
But still, you were so cool.

20:06.250 --> 20:10.000
Really? I was being too real,
I thought it was tacky as hell.

20:10.000 --> 20:11.630
What do you mean?

20:11.630 --> 20:13.750
That's what makes you awesome, Kiui.

20:16.580 --> 20:18.290
Yeah, maybe you're right.

20:20.920 --> 20:22.630
It's goodbye, world.

20:30.420 --> 20:31.380
What do you think?

20:32.630 --> 20:34.750
Nono-tan, these lyrics...

20:38.710 --> 20:39.830
I figured it out.

20:41.460 --> 20:43.250
Who I want to sing for.

20:45.380 --> 20:46.880
Can it, backseat gamer!

20:47.420 --> 20:49.750
I play the way I wanna play!

20:50.250 --> 20:55.420
That's right, because this guy is
the invincible VTuber Nox Ryugasaki!

20:56.210 --> 21:00.750
<b>Mei (#meeting · JELEE)
Nono-tan's lyrics are ready!</b>

20:56.580 --> 20:59.460
Nono-tan's lyrics are ready!

21:04.290 --> 21:05.630
Did you get those fixes done?

21:06.710 --> 21:13.040
So I have this childhood friend. A girl... and a boy,
who's just the coolest in the world.

21:13.290 --> 21:18.380
That friend created an ideal persona,
one that they're proud of,

21:18.960 --> 21:21.250
making it clear that they love who they are.

21:21.540 --> 21:24.830
I love that about my friend.

21:27.170 --> 21:29.460
And I want to be like that too.

21:30.580 --> 21:32.960
This is my art.

21:38.920 --> 21:42.630
This is my art I'm proud to say I love!

21:43.130 --> 21:46.130
<b>Mahiru Kouzuki
Yoru Umitsuki</b>

21:47.170 --> 21:51.960
That's completely different from what I ordered, and
you obviously don't know how to talk with respect.

21:53.670 --> 21:59.250
Still, it's true this is your art that I love.

22:00.750 --> 22:04.130
Good work. I promise to put on an incredible show.

22:04.750 --> 22:06.170
Exciting, isn't it?

22:10.630 --> 22:11.580
Hold on.

22:11.580 --> 22:12.420
Hmm?

22:15.170 --> 22:17.710
I want to negotiate something.

22:17.290 --> 22:18.790
<b>Music: Kimura
Lyrics:
To that sea where the snow falls</b>

22:18.920 --> 22:21.040
This event for the Sundolls at the end of the year...

22:22.130 --> 22:24.880
Won't you allow JELEE to perform there as well?

22:26.210 --> 22:29.920
The second hand won't stop, there's no time to be feeling down

22:29.920 --> 22:38.500
Every day is packed, a list full of things I want to do

22:38.710 --> 22:45.460
Talking takes too long so I'll make it brief with a song

22:45.670 --> 22:53.330
Ever since that night I found you, the rhythm started accelerating

22:55.710 --> 23:03.540
Only having 24 hours in a day isn't nearly enough

23:03.880 --> 23:10.540
I haven't caught up to the night yet and morning's already coming

23:10.670 --> 23:22.960
Just one hour more would do, I want to gaze
on that moon, the same moon as yours

23:23.170 --> 23:29.790
When I fell in love with the present that's ordinary
the future got a bit more vibrant

23:29.790 --> 23:35.330
That's how I waited for tomorrow
